    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d425">

                <pb facs="0527" n="1361" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1361"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 659.119/485</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Denmark</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grant-Smith</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Copenhagen</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-09-21T17:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 21, 1918, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 6.17 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2817. News of the signature of the United States-Danish agreement received with
                    general satisfaction and relief throughout Denmark. <pb facs="0528" n="1362"
                        xml:id="pg1362"/> During discussion with Foreign Minister yesterday I
                    suggested that a note of warning be sounded in the press against the expectation
                    of the immediate receipt of all the goods enumerated.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grant-Smith</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
